    "created_at": "2026-10-17T18:32:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-17T18:32:21Z",
    "body": "Came back to this, and it seems like the WebIDL footgun could be resolved by removing just the `move(USVString newEntryName)` overload, right?\r\n\r\nIf so, that should be fine, since any website using `move` in a cross-browser manner always needs to use the 2-argument `move(FileSystemDirectoryHandle destinationDirectory, USVString newEntryName)` overload anyway (since it's all that WebKit supports).\r\n\r\nWhat about an API which provides:\r\n1. A `move` method where the first argument is `FileSystemDirectoryHandle destinationDirectory` (with an overload for the optional second argument, the new filename)\r\n2. A `rename` method where the only argument is the new filename\r\n\r\nIf all three browser engines now support moving directory handles too, that API should (fingers crossed) be easy to ship just by updating the WebIDL.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fs/issues/comments/6238628744/reactions",
